tionalised. Many curries are found in the cuisines of countries in Southeast Asia and East Asia."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-curry"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Curry"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":1,"groups":[["Thai cuisine","cuisine/thai-cuisine",[["Green curry","dish/green-curry"]]]]},{"h":"Often cooked with","links":[["Coconut milk","ingredient/coconut-milk"],["Fish sauce","ingredient/fish-sauce"],["Kaffir lime","ingredient/kaffir-lime"],["Palm sugar","ingredient/palm-sugar"],["Thai basil","ingredient/thai-basil"],["Thai eggplant","ingredient/thai-eggplant"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/6/6f/Taj_Mahal_-_Lamb_Curry_Madras.jpg/500px-Taj_Mahal_-_Lamb_Curry_Madras.jpg","w":500,"h":375,"by":"Francesc Fort","lic":"CC BY-SA 4.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Taj_Mahal_-_Lamb_Curry_Madras.jpg"}},"ingredient/salsa-mexican-cuisine":{"t":"ingredient","r":"ingredient/salsa-mexican-cuisine","n":"Salsa (Mexican cuisine)","c":"#c9b8dd","crumb":[["Ingredients","ingredients"]],"sub":"Ingredient in 1 dish across 1 cuisine","intro":[["A salsa is any of a variety of sauces used as condiments for tacos and other Mexican and Mexican-American foods, and as dips for tortilla chips. They may be raw or cooked, and are generally served at room temperature."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-salsa-mexican-cuisine"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Salsa_(Mexican_cuisine)"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":1,"groups":[["Mexican cuisine","cuisine/mexican-cuisine",[["Huevos rancheros","dish/huevos-rancheros"]]]]},{"h":"Often cooked with","links":[["Avocado","ingredient/avocado"],["Chili pepper","ingredient/chili-pepper"],["Egg","ingredient/egg"],["Guacamole","ingredient/guacamole"],["Refried beans","ingredient/refried-beans"],["Tortilla","ingredient/tortilla"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/9/9c/Various_salsas.jpg/500px-Various_salsas.jpg","w":500,"h":281,"by":"Popo le Chien","lic":"CC BY-SA 3.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Various_salsas.jpg"}},"dish/italian-restaurant":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/italian-restaurant","n":"Italian restaurant","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish from Italian cuisine","dot":"#cf5f87","intro":[["Italian cuisine is a Mediterranean cuisine consisting of the ingredients, recipes and cooking techniques developed in Italy since Roman times, and later spread around the world together with waves of Italian diaspora. Significant changes occurred with the colonization of the Americas and the consequent introduction of potatoes, tomatoes, capsicums, and maize, as well as sugar beet—the latter introduced in quantity in the 18th century. Italian cuisine is one of the best-known and most widely appreciated worldwide. In 2025, Italian cuisine was listed as intangible cultural heritage by UNESCO."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-italian-restaurant"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Italian_restaurant"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Italian cuisine","cuisine/italian-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"Pasta Grannies","ref":"site/pastagrannies-substack-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"pastagrannies.substack.com","note":"Vicky Bennison's long-running video series filming Italian grandmothers making regional pasta by hand.","url":"https://pastagrannies.substack.com/p/pasta-grannies-is-now-on-substack","suggested":true,"kind":"youtube"},{"name":"Recipes from Italy","ref":"site/recipesfromitaly-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"recipesfromitaly.com","note":"Traditional Italian recipes written by Italian home cooks, organized by region and course.","url":"https://recipesfromitaly.com","suggested":true,"kind":"blog"},{"name":"Manu's Menu","ref":"site/manusmenu-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"manusmenu.com","note":"Italian-born home cook Manuela sharing classic family and regional Italian dishes.","url":"https://www.manusmenu.com/about/about-this-site","suggested":true,"kind":"blog"}]},{"h":"More from Italian cuisine","links":[["Acquacotta","dish/acquacotta"],["Agliata","dish/agliata"],["Agnolotti","dish/agnolotti"],["Antipasto","dish/antipasto"],["Arancini","dish/arancini"],["Biscotti","dish/biscotti"],["Bolinhos de bacalhau","dish/bolinhos-de-bacalhau"],["Bombolone","dish/bombolone"],["Budino","dish/budino"],["Cabbage roll","dish/cabbage-roll"],["Caesar salad","dish/caesar-salad"],["Cannelloni","dish/cannelloni"],["Capellini","dish/capellini"],["Carbonara","dish/carbonara"],["Carpaccio","dish/carpaccio"],["Cassatella di sant'Agata","dish/cassatella-di-sant-agata"],["Cassoeula","dish/cassoeula"],["Ciabatta","dish/ciabatta"],["Cioppino","dish/cioppino"],["Coda alla vaccinara","dish/coda-alla-vaccinara"],["Colomba pasquale","dish/colomba-pasquale"],["Conti roll","dish/conti-roll"],["Cotoletta alla bolognese","dish/cotoletta-alla-bolognese"],["Crostata","dish/crostata"],["Drago restaurants","dish/drago-restaurants"],["Focaccia pugliese","dish/focaccia-pugliese"],["Frittata","dish/frittata"],["Giardiniera","dish/giardiniera"],["Guanciale","dish/guanciale"],["Italian wedding soup","dish/italian-wedding-soup"],["Lampredotto","dish/lampredotto"],["Lasagna","dish/lasagna"],["List of Italian restaurants","dish/list-of-italian-restaurants"],["Marinara sauce","dish/marinara-sauce"],["Mondeghili","dish/mondeghili"],["Paccheri","dish/paccheri"],["Panini (sandwich)","dish/panini-sandwich"],["Panna cotta","dish/panna-cotta"],["Passatelli","dish/passatelli"],["Pecorino","dish/pecorino"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/d/df/Italian_food.JPG/500px-Italian_food.JPG","w":500,"h":500,"by":"Various: ElfQrin (Valerio Capello) for File:Eq it-na pizza-margherita sep2005 sml.jpg Ed…","lic":"CC BY-SA 4.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Italian_food.JPG"}},"ingredient/spanish-mackerel":{"t":"ingredient","r":"ingredient/spanish-mackerel","n":"Spanish mackerel","c":"#c9b8dd","crumb":[["Ingredients","ingredients"]],"sub":"Ingredient in 2 dishes across 1 cuisine","intro":[["Scomberomorini is a tribe of ray-finned, saltwater, bony fishes that is commonly known as Spanish mackerels, seerfishes, or seer fish. This tribe is a subset of the mackerel family (Scombridae), which it shares with four sister tribes, the tunas, mackerels, bonitos, and butterfly kingfish. Scomberomorini comprises 21 species across three genera. They are pelagic fish, fast swimmers and predatory in nature, that fight vigorously when caught. They are mainly caught using hooks and lines."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-spanish-mackerel"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Spanish_mackerel"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":1,"groups":[["Indonesian cuisine","cuisine/indonesian-cuisine",[["Kemplang","dish/kemplang"],["Otak-otak","dish/otak-otak"]]]]},{"h":"Often cooked with","links":[["Tapioca flour","ingredient/tapioca-flour"],["Wahoo","ingredient/wahoo"],["Banana leaf","ingredient/banana-leaf"],["Bird's eye chili","ingredient/bird-s-eye-chili"],["Candlenut","ingredient/candlenut"],["Caraway seed","ingredient/caraway-seed"],["Chili pepper","ingredient/chili-pepper"],["Coconut milk","ingredient/coconut-milk"],["Egg","ingredient/egg"],["Galangal","ingredient/galangal"],["Ginger","ingredient/ginger"],["Grated coconut","ingredient/grated-coconut"],["Leaves","ingredient/leaves"],["Milkfish","ingredient/milkfish"],["Scallion","ingredient/scallion"],["Shallot","ingredient/shallot"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/7/75/Screg_u0.gif/500px-Screg_u0.gif","w":500,"h":375,"by":"Unknown author","lic":"Public domain","licUrl":"","page":"ht